*=============================================================================
* FL.SUNBIZ.CORP.DATA
*
* Fixed-width column layout equates for the Florida SunBiz "Corporate Data
* File" (record length 1440 characters; data rows have NO header row).
* Source: FL-SunBiz-Corp+AltName-File-Layout.xlsx, sheet 'SunBiz-Corporate'.
*
* OpenQM's EQU statement parses an unquoted comma in the value as starting
* a NEW 'name TO value' pair (EQU name TO value [, name TO value ...]), so
* a single 'start,length' value per field does not compile. Each field is
* therefore two scalar equates, .POS and .LEN, used together:
*   LINE[CORPORATION.NAME.POS, CORPORATION.NAME.LEN]   ->   LINE[13, 192]
*
* Naming rule: the equate token is the layout's Field Name with spaces
* replaced by '.' (BASIC identifiers cannot contain '-'). The DICT item
* name for each field is the same Field Name with spaces replaced by '-'
* instead - i.e. derived from the equate token by swapping '.' for '-'.
* Exception: 'Zip+4' fields use '.' in place of '+' too (not a space, but
* '+' is likewise illegal in a BASIC token); use 'ZIP+4' literally for the
* DICT name for those fields.
*
* Duplicate 'Filler' fields in the source layout are numbered FILLER.1..4
* to keep equate tokens unique; use 'FILLER' (unnumbered) as their DICT name
* if a placeholder DICT item is ever needed.
*
* Contains fields for up to 6 officers, starting at field 37; each officer
* block repeats the same 7 sub-fields (Title/Type/Name/Address/City/State/
* Zip+4).
*=============================================================================

EQU CORPORATION.NUMBER.POS       TO 1
EQU CORPORATION.NUMBER.LEN       TO 12
EQU CORPORATION.NAME.POS         TO 13
EQU CORPORATION.NAME.LEN         TO 192
EQU STATUS.POS                   TO 205
